# Line-ending stability for markdown only, added 2026-10-08 on the user's
# "only if it breaks nothing" instruction after measuring the tree: of the 235
# tracked markdown files under docs/ the working copies read 126 CRLF-only, 91
# LF-only and 18 mixed, so the file on disk is the artefact reviews digest and it
# must never be silently rewritten. `-text` disables every EOL conversion in both
# directions: git stores the bytes a lane actually wrote, and a checkout never
# changes a document that has already been measured.
#
# Deliberately NOT a repo-wide rule. data/*.json, *.html, *.js and every other
# *.json stay `unspecified` and under core.autocrlf, because the live feed writer
# pushes data/*.json and the dashboard artefacts on a 15-minute cadence and nothing
# may renormalise them.
*.md -text

# Review evidence packages keep their bytes for the same reason, added
# 2026-10-11: docs/review/ holds files copied verbatim from an external reviewer
# and their SHA-256 values are recorded in docs/CHANGELOG.md and in the package's
# own README, so a later checkout must not renormalise them. Scoped to that one
# folder on purpose; the rule above still covers markdown everywhere else and
# nothing else in the tree changes.
docs/review/** -text

# Byte-exact research artefacts, added 2026-10-15 with the USD brief handoff.
# `docs/research/handoff/usd/v1/HANDOFF_MANIFEST.json` records the sha256 of every generated
# brief, the local Research Library registry records the same hash for each of the same 25
# files, and `tests/research_handoff.test.js` compares the archive's members with the files on
# disk. `-text` disables line-ending conversion in both directions, so a checkout hands back the
# bytes the builder wrote and one hash keeps meaning the same thing on every machine. Scoped to
# this folder, which this commit introduces; no path that already ships is covered.
docs/research/handoff/** -text
